      "content": "Tax agencies employ specialized cross-border audits, leveraging shared intelligence networks like the Common Reporting Standard (CRS) to automatically exchange financial data between nations, which makes hiding assets in shell companies extremely difficult. Investigators often use forensic accounting techniques to trace layered ownership structures and can subpoena banks or remain centers to reveal true beneficiaries behind anonymous trusts. Consequently, attempting to conceal assets often results in aggressive enforcement actions, including back-pay taxes, statutory penalties, and potentially criminal prosecution for evasion.",
